NOTES:

    This system has been built from the ground up, and NO DSN patches
  are to be installed.  All patches have been installed at source code level.

    All the files on this disk have been modified, and are no longer
  compatable with other versions of OS78.  Mixing OS278 files with OS78
  files can affect the operation of the system; destroy the system disk;
  and or the data disk.  Use HELP to aid in the use of the OS278 system.

    Documentation is never perfect or complete.  Trying to document a system
  without writing a manual isn't easy.  However the documentation supplied
  should help in using most of the enhancements.  If you do need a manual
  refer to OS/78 User's Manual (order # AA-5748C-TA).  Remember that any
  documentation on this disk supersedes the OS/78 manual.


							Enjoy

Some notes on OS278

DISK 1 of 3 contains all system files, and development tools
DISK 2 of 3 contains Basic, and Fortran 4
DISK 3 of 3 is the OS278 winchester install disk.

HARD DISK INSTALL installs OS278 on your hard disk by allocating a
	volume called OS278.  This supports the devices RX50:, RX51:,
	RD50;, RD51:, RD52:, RD53:

	To install OS278 on the winchester simply boot the floppy
	(disk 3 of 3) and follow the directions.

MONITOR -

	o Can accept lower case input

DUPLICATE - 

	o Not compatible with OS278.  (File RXCOPY.SV has been removed)
	o All formatting is now done by FORMAT.SV.

RX01/02 -

	o Device names have changed from RXA0-3 to RX20-3.
	o The new RX handlers not compatable with original RX handlers.

CCL.SV, SET.SV, MONITOR -

	o not compatable with previous versions of OS78/OS278.
	o Any attempt to mix OS278 utilities with OS78 utilities
	  will corrupt your disk.

SETUP.SV -

	o For DECmate II only.  This invokes the user selection menu.

WPFLOP.SV -

	o Has many fixes over version 3.0.

	o When editing a file in WPS that has just been transfered
	  from OS278 press GOLD ADVANCE.  This will align the text
	  to the current ruler setting.  This only needs to be done
	  once.

LPTS.HN -

	o This handler now accepts SET LPT WIDTH command.
	o Modifications have been made to pass 7 bit characters,
	  and all control codes.

FUTIL.SV, BATCH.SV -

	o Has been modified to allow patching under BATCH control.
	o Batch, system commands must be in upper case.

CREF.SV -

	o The CREF literal table has been fixed.

HELP.SV, HELP.HL -

	o The help file reflects the changes made to this system.

BASIC system -

	o Refer to the BASIC.TX file for the enhancements.
	o Note: The AND, OR instructions have been removed.

RENUM.BA -

	o Replaces RESEQ.BA, requires this system for operation.
	  List the program for operation procedures.

EDIT.SV -

	o Virtual text editor.  Refer to EDTHLP.TX file.

	o Note: On occasion when editing near the end of the file
	  the editor will display one line twice.  This will occur
	  at the bottom of the screen.  If this happens press GOLD R
	  to refresh the screen.  This is a bug.  However we feel that
	  the advantages of the editor outweigh this one problem, so
	  we decided to leave it on the system.

	  For those of you who prefer to use the old OS78 EDIT or TECO
	  with VTEDIT for the VT100 this system will not restrict the
	  operation.

MOUNT.SV -

	o Mounts a hard disk volume on designated RD50:, RD51:,
	  RD52:, or RD53:.  Syntax:

	Modates volumes of any 8kbyte multiple
	  size up to the capacity of the disk.  Traditionally, OS278
	  has regarded the hard disk to be of fixed 4096 block size.
	  When the Hard Disk Utility under Master Menu allocates an
	  OS278 volume, it creates a directory that has the proper
	  empty space entry for the size of the volume - whatever the
	  size may be.  When the OS278 SQUISH or ZERO commands are
	  invoked, however, the last directory empty entry is set so
	  that the total number of blocks on the disk is 4096.  FIXDIR
	  sizes the disk by reading its hard disk volume directory
	  entry and then adjusts the OS278 directory so that things
	  add up.

	  FIXDIR vname

	       or

	  R FIXDIR vname

MENU.SV -

	  This command will boot the master menu volume.	


Disk 3 of 3  OS278 winchester install disk -

	After OS278 has been installed on the winchester the startup
	volume is set to the OS278 system.  If you wish to reset the
	startup volume to Master Menu follow the below instructions.

	Boot the winchester.
	At the OS278 system prompt enter the CCL command MENU.
	Master Menu is now active.  Enter date.
	Select the HD (Hard Disk) services menu.
	Press NEXT SCREEN.
	Select the S option (Select startup volume).
	Enter the volume name MENU as the startup volume. 
	Master Menu is now marked at the startup volume.

